      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 65-year-old man who had previously undergone multiple stenting on the coronary tree, was referred for urgent surgery. The left anterior descending coronary artery was found to be completely stented from the proximal to the distal portion. Open endarterectomy was required for removal of multiple thrombosed stents and reconstruction of the left anterior descending artery using left internal mammary artery. This highlights the need to spare the distal parts of coronary vessels for future surgery."},
